        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Have you noticed that in areas like smartphones and chips, China’s top tech video creators often go much deeper technically than tech media in many other countries?\n\nTake Geekerwan, for example. I still rarely see media elsewhere analyze a mobile chip’s performance, power consumption, and architecture in such depth.\n\nThe same goes for teardowns. Lou Bin (WekiHome / @ Wekihome9414) goes far beyond simply taking a phone apart, diving deep into its internal structure, components, and the engineering principles behind the design.\n\nI’ve always wondered: why has China produced so many tech creators capable of going this incredibly deep? What do you think is the reason?"
        },
